WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.210
Everything warm glows.

2
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:04.750
You just can't see it.

3
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:10.410
This is DIY-Thermocam V4.

4
00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:12.670
A thermal camera you build yourself.

5
00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:16.770
At its heart sits a FLIR Lepton.

6
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.600
It has nineteen thousand two hundred pixels,

7
00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:23.230
and every one of them measures a temperature,

8
00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:26.150
from minus ten to four hundred fifty degrees.

9
00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.350
The new V4 board comes fully assembled.

10
00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:32.560
No soldering.

11
00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:36.340
Plug in the Lepton, the Teensy, the battery

12
00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:37.750
and the touchscreen.

13
00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:39.810
Eight screws close the shell.

14
00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:45.100
Print the shell yourself, or have it cut from

15
00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.100
acrylic.

16
00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:48.010
Both come from the same design files.

17
00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:53.580
Switch it on, and Firmware 4.0 opens straight

18
00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:54.850
into the live image.

19
00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:59.130
The hottest spot, the coldest spot and the center,

20
00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.630
measured almost nine times a second.

21
00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:07.730
Nineteen color palettes.

22
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.000
Three themes.

23
00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:13.210
Everything else is one tap away:

24
00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:16.090
set the range, place your own measuring spots,

25
00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:18.700
record photos and video, and look back in the

26
00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:19.700
gallery.

27
00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.730
Find the overloaded breaker.

28
00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.290
The drafty window.

29
00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:26.630
The one part that runs too hot.

30
00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:31.120
With the larger battery, it runs for up to six

31
00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:34.490
hours, and it charges over USB-C.

32
00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:39.260
Plug in one cable, and DIY-Thermocam Studio

33
00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:42.270
shows the same image live on your computer.

34
00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:46.880
Draw regions, set alarms, and export your recordings,

35
00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:49.370
on Mac, Windows and Linux.

36
00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:54.500
All parts, including the sensor, come to just

37
00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:56.530
under three hundred dollars.

38
00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:02.470
The board, the shell, the firmware and Studio:

39
00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:05.430
every file is yours to read and change.

40
00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:11.530
Build your own at diy-thermocam.net.
